  "label": "The Brits gave up their guns",
  "description": "The top text 'the brits gave up their guns' is mapped onto the visual entities of Queen Elizabeth II and Prince Charles, who are depicted as symbols of the British government and monarchy. The meme uses their image to represent the British state or populace, implying that the government (embodied by the monarchy) is responsible for the policy of gun control (or its perceived abandonment) and the subsequent enforcement of TV licensing laws. This is an analogical mapping where the visual material (the seated monarchs) is projected as the 'Brits' or the entity being referred to in the text.",
